PART A — COMPLETE SETTINGS MODULE

2. Appearance and Flashcard Direction

2.1 Theme

Provide a theme selector with:

* Light mode
* Dark mode

Requirements:

* Default: Light mode.
* Apply the selected theme throughout the application.
* Persist the selection across reloads and application restarts.
* Ensure text, cards, dialogs, forms, and controls remain readable in both themes.

2.2 Default Flashcard Direction

Provide three options:

* German → Persian
* Persian → German
* Random direction

Use these internal values:

* de
* fa
* rand

Default: de.

The random option must select a direction independently for each flashcard. Do not choose one direction for the entire session and reuse it for every card.

3. Daily Learning Limits and Session Order

3.1 New Words per Day

* Setting key: nw
* Numeric range: 0–500
* Default: 10

3.2 Reviews per Day

* Setting key: rv
* Numeric range: 0–500
* Default: 20

A value of zero must be handled consistently and must not accidentally cause an unlimited session unless that behavior is explicitly defined and communicated in the UI.

3.3 Session Order

Setting key: order.

Options:

* due: Review due cards first, then introduce new words.
* new: Introduce new words first.
* mix: Alternate between review cards and new words.
* rand: Randomize the order of eligible cards.

Default: due.

Make sure the actual study-session scheduler respects the selected option.

3.4 Category Filters

Setting key: activeCats.

Allow users to select which vocabulary categories participate in the daily learning session.

Requirements:

* Generate the category list dynamically from the application’s existing category data.
* If no category is selected, include all categories.
* Apply the filter to the daily study session without deleting or modifying excluded vocabulary.
* Do not unexpectedly apply this setting to unrelated vocabulary-management screens.

4. Review Algorithm and Difficult Words

4.1 Review Interval Adjustment

Setting key: ivlMod.

Options:

* 0.8: Strict mode — shorter review intervals.
* 1.0: Normal mode.
* 1.25: Relaxed mode — longer review intervals.

Default: 1.0.

This setting must affect the actual scheduling algorithm, not just the displayed interface. Apply it consistently while preserving the application’s existing spaced-repetition logic.

Prevent invalid, negative, or non-finite intervals.

4.2 Difficult-Word Threshold

Setting key: leechN.

* Numeric range: 2–20
* Default: 4

Use this value as the configurable repeated-error threshold.

The existing application identifies a difficult word using the configured error threshold and an error ratio of at least 40%. Preserve that logic unless inspection reveals a bug requiring correction.

4.3 Difficult-Word Action

Setting key: leechAct.

Options:

* mark: Mark the word as difficult without suspending it.
* suspend: Mark the word and exclude it from daily study and review sessions.

Default: mark.

Suspended words must remain available in vocabulary management and must not be deleted.

5. Flashcard Timer

5.1 Automatic Answer Reveal

Setting key: revealSec.

* Range: 0–120 seconds
* Default: 0
* Zero disables automatic reveal.

If enabled, reveal the answer for the current flashcard after the configured delay.

Critical requirements:

* The timer must belong to the current card only.
* Cancel or reset it when changing cards, restarting a session, closing the study view, or navigating away.
* Never reveal the answer of a different card because of a timer started for a previous card.
* Do not allow multiple stale timers to interfere with the current card.

5.2 Show Study Timer

Setting key: showTimer.

* Default: false

When enabled, display the timer in the study interface. When disabled, hide it without disrupting the study session.

6. Pronunciation and Audio Settings

6.1 Automatic Pronunciation

Setting key: auto.

* Default: false

When enabled, automatically pronounce the German vocabulary word at the appropriate point in the flashcard workflow.

6.2 Read the Example Sentence

Setting key: autoEx.

* Default: false

When enabled, read the example sentence after pronouncing the vocabulary word, when an example exists.

Avoid overlapping speech and cancel outdated speech when the current card changes.

6.3 German Accent

Setting key: vreg.

Options:

* Automatic/default: ""
* German (Germany): de-DE
* German (Austria): de-AT
* German (Switzerland): de-CH

Default: "".

Use a compatible installed speech voice where possible. If the exact requested accent is unavailable, fall back gracefully and do not crash.

6.4 Voice Selection

Setting key: voice.

* Default: automatic voice selection.
* Populate the list using available German speech-synthesis voices.
* Refresh the list when voices become available asynchronously.
* Restore the selected voice when possible.
* Handle unavailable or removed voices gracefully.

6.5 Speech Rate

Setting key: rate.

* Range: 0.5–1.1
* Step: 0.05
* Default: 0.85

Apply the selected rate to all relevant pronunciation actions.

6.6 Test Voice

Provide a functional “Test Voice” button that speaks:

“Guten Tag! Ich lerne Deutsch in Wien.”

The test must use the selected voice, accent preference, and speech rate.

Retain concise compatibility guidance for iOS/iPadOS, Android, Windows, and macOS.

7. Daily Goal and Backup Reminder

7.1 Daily Goal

Setting key: goal.

* Range: 0–500
* Default: 20
* Zero disables the goal.

Track daily progress accurately and reset the daily count according to the application’s existing date-handling logic.

7.2 Backup Reminder Frequency

Setting key: bkDays.

Options:

* 0: Disabled
* 3: Every 3 days
* 7: Every 7 days
* 14: Every 14 days
* 30: Every 30 days

Default: 7.

Persist the last relevant backup/reminder timestamp if necessary. Avoid repeatedly showing the same reminder during every render or navigation event.

Do not claim that a backup has been created unless the application actually creates one.

